"B234-09","when":"August 2005","p":3,"h":"The President – Gerry North"},{"id":"B237-02","when":"November 2005","p":1,"h":"Road Relay Glory"},{"id":"B248-03","when":"October 2006","p":1,"h":"Road Running: The season starts with a win"},{"id":"B249-08","when":"October 2006","p":3,"h":"Hon. Secretary’s Report to AGM 2006"},{"id":"B252-05","when":"January 2007","p":2,"h":"Skipper’s Corner"},{"id":"B253-07","when":"February 2007","p":2,"h":"Bels in subdued mood on the Common"},{"id":"B260-09","when":"No. 260","p":4,"h":"Hon. Secretary’s Report to AGM 2007"},{"id":"B263-08","when":"No. 263","p":3,"h":"Mud, blood & guts at “Parly” Hill"},{"id":"B263-16","when":"No. 263","p":7,"h":"From The Belgravian"},{"id":"B267-08","when":"No. 267","p":4,"h":"Double win in the Surrey Road Relays"},{"id":"B269-02","when":"No. 269","p":1,"h":"South of Thames Champs – a 14th win"}],"photos":[{"f":"crops/B157/B157-p23-sunday-morning-at-arthurs.jpg","c":"SUNDAY MORNING AT ARTHUR'S Some of the \"gang\" enjoying refreshments---and Ron Linstead's clowning---on the lawn of Lauriston Cottage. L. to R. (rear)Charlie Dabbs, Charlie Smart,Trevor Hart,Ron Mitchell,Arthur Bruce,Howard Satchell,Ron Linstead,Mel Thorpe,John Thresher. L. to R. (front)Peter Wrench,John Dear,Gordon Biscoe,Charlie Manning.","id":"B157-49","w":"November 1965"},{"f":"crops/B255/B255-p01-national-road-relay-team.jpg","c":"Happy with a seventh successive year in the medals at the National Road Relay. Standing (left to right) Gerry North, Gordon Biscoe, Bill Laws, Brian Pritchard, Tom Osment, Maureen Pritchard, Zara Chidoub, Mark Pollard, Jonathan Blackledge, Janet Blackledge, Mike Blackledge, Neil Speaight, Alan Mead, Padraic Buckley, Paul Freary, Eric Hall, Pete Willis, Hazel Mead. Front row. Mavis Hall, Charles Jones, Richard Ward, Simon Jones, Malachi Byansi, Will Cockerell, Pat Mead, Phil Wicks.","id":"B255-02","w":"May 2007"},{"f":"crops/B172/B172-p44-gordon-biscoe-cup.jpg","c":"","id":"B172-84","w":"December 1969"},{"f":"crops/B177/B177-p04-biscoe-ashford.jpg","c":"This is the magazine they cannot gag. Boldly, the Belgravian brings you this picture which proves that cross country officials do not officiate only in blizzards of the monsoon season.\n\nEveryone knows what a mountain of work for Belgrave grimacing Gordon Biscoe (left) gets through. Fewer may know what an invaluable asset we have in our assistant hon. secretary, Bill Ashford, seen here with his recorder's board at the Blackstaffe Shield.","id":"B177-07","w":"June 1971"},{"f":"crops/B209/B209-p07-gordon-biscoe.jpg","c":"","id":"B209-14","w":"October 1985"},{"f":"crops/B210/B210-p53-richard-ohara-800m.jpg","c":"Gordon Biscoe appears to be looking at the watch in disbelief but it was a comfortable 58 at the bell for Richard O'Hara who ran out an easy winner. Alan Painter, a youngster of 39, was the only other runner inside 2 minutes. Pat Lyttle is still in touch at this point but his legs are about to part company with the rest of his body any second!","id":"B210-42","w":"October 1986"},{"f":"crops/B217/B217-p29-heathfield-biscoe-davies.jpg","c":"Jim Heathfield and Gordon Biscoe get a quote for \"The Belgravian\" from sage John Davies.","id":"B217-105","w":"December 1991"},{"f":"crops/B221/B221-p09-young-athletes-1970s.jpg","c":"Above: The 70s and a photo call after a Young Athletes Sunday morning training session at Wimbledon Park. The adults, left of the group, left to right are: John Martin, Frank Simmons, Jim Heathfield (crouching), Bob Taylor, Reg. Hopkins Jnr., Reg Hopkins Snr. And on the right: John Baker, Philip Gee, Peter Hilliar, Gordon Biscoe, Mickey Pyer, Gordon Doubleday, Alan Mead and Bill Couzens.","id":"B221-23","w":"Winter 1993/94"},{"f":"crops/B227/B227-p10-officials-battersea.jpg","c":"The officials, pictured left, were (from the top left to right): Gordon Biscoe (timekeeper), John Sullivan (North London timekeeper), Don Anderson (timekeeper), Yak Stegner (Herne Hill timekeeper), Terry Earle (timekeeper), Pat Mead (track referee), Stuart Bennett (track judge), Bob Bridges (timekeeper), Richard Biscoe (track judge), Alan Mead (chief timekeeper), Leslie Earle (track judge). Not pictured but recording entries and assisting with the seeding was John Jeffery while starter was Bob Bush (Serpentine).","id":"B227-25","w":"March 1999"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B157/B157-p23-sunday-morning-at-arthurs.jpg","caption":"SUNDAY MORNING AT ARTHUR'S Some of the \"gang\" enjoying refreshments---and Ron Linstead's clowning---on the lawn of Lauriston Cottage. L. to R. (rear)Charlie Dabbs, Charlie Smart,Trevor Hart,Ron Mitchell,Arthur Bruce,Howard Satchell,Ron Linstead,Mel Thorpe,John Thresher. L. to R. (front)Peter Wrench,John Dear,Gordon Biscoe,Charlie Manning.","source":"B157-49","when":"November 1965"},"x":1,"share":{"d":"Gordon Biscoe in The Belgravian, the Belgrave Harriers club gazette, 1954–2007: 103 mentions in 60 issues, 43 race results and 9 photographs. Wrote or reported 43 items.","img":"https://belgravian-images.stephendgardner.workers.dev/belgravian/crops/B172/B172-p44-gordon-biscoe-cup.jpg","u":"https://stephengardner1.github.io/belgrave-harriers-data/belgravian/read/share/p-gordon-biscoe.html"},"legend":false}